chuck <chucko@nil.car> writes:

> Nethack is started (in unix) by a script which then runs the binary. The 
> binary IS root execute only and the save files are root write only.

No it isn't. Yes, it's started by a script that runs the binary, but
nothing quoted above after it is true, unless somebody has fucked up the
installation.
By default, the permissions and ownership are like here:
-rwsr-xr-x  1 games bin 1723170 Aug 25  2004 /usr/games/lib/nethackdir/nethack
Nothing referring to root here.

Notice that it CAN be installed sgid instead of suid, but the default in
the installation script is suid games.
You should NEVER install ANY game suid root, and nethack is no exception
to that rule.

